---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Why these figures differ from others" activeNav="differences">
  <Fragment slot="masthead">
    <h1>Why these figures differ from others</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Two sources can both be right and still give different numbers, because they count different things. This
      page says what each one counts. It does not try to make the figures match.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Registrations are not sales</h2>
    <p>
      A vehicle is counted in the month it was first registered, not the month it was ordered, paid for or handed
      over. A vehicle can be registered before it is sold.{" "}
      <a href="/method#data-grains">What the charts count</a>.{" "}
      <a href="/caveats">Registered is not the same as sold</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Survivors are not registrations</h2>
    <p>
      The charts count vehicles first registered in a month that are still registered at the latest snapshot.
      Vehicles that have left the register since are not in the count, so a count for an older month is smaller than the
      number first registered then. <a href="/method#data-grains">The three ways to count the register</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Scope can differ</h2>
    <p>
      This site counts only some vehicle types, and only vehicles registered in New Zealand for the first time.
      A source that counts other types, or counts returning vehicles, will give a different total.{" "}
      <a href="/method#vehicle-scope">Which vehicles are counted</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The Motor Industry Association counts differently</h2>
    <p>
      The Motor Industry Association (MIA) counts vehicles delivered to buyers. Its figures are not open data, so
      this site cannot check them or line them up with its own, and it does not adjust its figures to match.
    </p>

    <h2>Other sites take a different source</h2>
    <p>
      Some other sites take first registrations from NZTA's registrations dashboard rather than from the open
      register this site reads. They count what that dashboard counts. This site does not claim to match them.{" "}
      <a href="/caveats">Other limits of the data</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>If a figure here still looks wrong</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/feedback">Report it</a>, with the page address and the figure you expected.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
